# --- @fill: time telling (Véierel vir / op / hallwer) --------------------------
# Distractors are the other two time-telling words — the three-way confusion
# (quarter to / quarter past / half past) is the core A1 clock drill.

@fill
@lu Et ass [Véierel vir] sechs.
@en It's [quarter to] six.
@distractor-lu Véierel op
@distractor-lu hallwer
@distractor-lu fënnef vir
@distractor-en quarter past
@distractor-en half past
@distractor-en five to

@fill
@lu Et ass [Véierel op] dräi.
@en It's [quarter past] three.
@distractor-lu Véierel vir
@distractor-lu hallwer
@distractor-lu fënnef op
@distractor-en quarter to
@distractor-en half past
@distractor-en five past

@fill
@lu Et ass [hallwer] véier.
@en It is [half past] three.
@distractor-lu Véierel vir
@distractor-lu Véierel op
@distractor-lu fënnef op
@distractor-en quarter to
@distractor-en quarter past
@distractor-en five past

# --- @fill: prepositions of time and place ------------------------------------
# um (at a clock time) vs. am (in the month) vs. virum (in front of) — the
# contracted forms this level teaches.

@fill
@lu Ech gi [um] siwen Auer lafe.
@en I go running [at] seven o'clock.
@distractor-lu am
@distractor-lu vum
@distractor-lu beim
@distractor-en in
@distractor-en from
@distractor-en by

@fill
@lu Mir treffe [virum] Kino.
@en We meet [in front of the] cinema.
@distractor-lu am
@distractor-lu beim
@distractor-lu um
@distractor-en at the
@distractor-en by the
@distractor-en in the

@fill
